  "body": "I'm trying to program a **react-pwa** that uses the **serial api**.\r\nTo use streams i add _'@stardazed/streams'_ and _'@stardazed/streams-text-encoding'_ via yarn.\r\nbut i get this error:\r\n_Uncaught (in promise) TypeError: Failed to execute 'pipeThrough' on 'ReadableStream': member readable is not of type ReadableStream._\r\n***\r\nCode (simplyfied):\r\n```\r\nclass MyTransformer {\r\n  constructor() {\r\n    this.chunks = '';\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  start() {\r\n    this.chunks = '';\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  transform(chunk, controller) {\r\n    this.chunks += chunk;\r\n    const lines = this.chunks.split(\"\\r\\n\");\r\n    this.chunks = lines.pop();\r\n    lines.forEach((line) => controller.enqueue(line));\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  flush(controller) {\r\n    controller.enqueue(this.chunks);\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n\r\nasync function onClick() {\r\n    port = await navigator.serial.requestPort();\r\n    await port.open({ baudRate: 115200 });\r\n\r\n    const decoder = new TextDecoderStream();\r\n    const stream = port.readable;\r\n\r\n    const inputDone = stream.pipeTo(decoder.writable);\r\n    const inputStream = decoder.readable.pipeThrough(new TransformStream(new MyTransformer()));\r\n\r\n    let reader = inputStream.getReader();\r\n    writer = port.writable.getWriter();\r\n\r\n    readLoop(reader);\r\n  }\r\n```\r\n",
